---
import Layout from "@layouts/ComponentsLayout.astro";
---

<Layout>
  <h1 class="govuk-heading-xl">Tag</h1>
  <p class="govuk-body-l">
    The Tag component indicates the status of something, such as an item on a
    task list or a phase banner
  </p>

  <h2 class="govuk-heading-l">Example</h2>
  <strong class="govuk-tag"> Alpha </strong>

  <!-- GOVUK_GUIDANCE:START (auto-generated - edited content will be overwritten by scripts/update-component-guidance.mjs) -->
  <h2 class="govuk-heading-l">When to use this component</h2>
  <p class="govuk-body">
    Use the Tag component when it’s possible for something to have more than one
    status and it’s useful for the user to know about that status. For example,
    you can use a tag to show whether an item in a <a
      class="govuk-link"
      href="https://design-system.service.gov.uk/components/task-list/"
      >Task list component</a
    > has been ‘completed’.
  </p>
  <!-- GOVUK_GUIDANCE:END -->
</Layout>
